<title>THAILAND: SIAM PULP SCRAPS INDONESIAN PLANT PLAN.</title>
<headline>SIAM PULP SCRAPS INDONESIAN PLANT PLAN.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai paper company Siam Pulp and Paper said on Thursday it has scrapped plans to build a pulp and paper plant in Indonesia.</p>
<p>Siam Pulp said in a statement filed with the Stock Exchange of Thailand that it would form a joint venture, Nityasa Prima, with Suryaraya Wahana Co, a subsidiary of Indonesia's Astra International PT, to build a 13 billion baht ($42 million) plant in Kalimantan.</p>
<p>Siam Pulp had a 30 percent stake in the Nityasa Prima project and Suryaraya Wahana owned 60 percent.</p>
<p>($1 = 31 baht)</p>
